@startuml
title Aztec transaction lifecycle — private first, then public, then settlement
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam LifelineBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

actor User
participant "Wallet" as W
participant "PXE\n(client device)" as PXE
participant "Aztec node\n/ sequencer" as SEQ
participant "Prover\nnetwork" as PRV
participant "Rollup contract\n(Ethereum L1)" as L1

User -> W : transfer 10 tokens privately
W -> PXE : simulate the entrypoint
PXE -> SEQ : fetch tagged logs, tree roots
SEQ --> PXE : encrypted logs and roots
PXE -> PXE : trial-decrypt, select notes,\nexecute private functions
note over PXE #F5F9FF
  Arguments, notes and the call stack
  stay on the device. The simulation
  runs kernel-less, so no signature
  is requested yet.
end note
W -> PXE : proveTx with authwits
PXE -> PXE : run the kernel circuits\ninit, inner, reset, tail
PXE -> SEQ : proof + note hashes + nullifiers\n+ enqueued public calls
note over PXE, SEQ #F5F9FF
  What crosses this line: commitments,
  nullifiers, encrypted logs, and every
  public call with its arguments in clear.
end note
SEQ -> SEQ : verify the private proof
SEQ -> SEQ : execute enqueued public calls\nin the AVM, update public state
SEQ -> L1 : publish the block\n+ data to blobs
SEQ -> PRV : delegate epoch proving
PRV -> PRV : rollup circuits\ntx, block, checkpoint, epoch
PRV -> L1 : submit the epoch proof
L1 -> L1 : verify, then finalise\nthe state transition
L1 --> W : settled
@enduml
